  "name": "Future rainfall and building-level pluvial flood risk in Logroño",
  "description": "Does heavier future rainfall put more residents of Logroño (Spain) in buildings at pluvial flood risk? Using the result tables of the Logroño flood-adaptation scenarios analysis (v0.1.0), this repository compares present and future (EURO-CORDEX median and 90th percentile) REACHOUT design rainfall, with the current green cover, for every return period from 2 to 200 years, and checks the future rainfall against the Destination Earth Climate DT. It holds one FORRT nanopublication chain (question-rooted) and its headline figure.",
